  "question": {
    "text": "The compound formed by the reaction of ethanal with semicarbazide contains _______ number of nitrogen atoms.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "03",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><b>Semicarbazide</b> is the chemical compound with the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>OC</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math>. It is a water-soluble white solid. It is a derivative of urea.</p><p>Acetaldehyde reacts with semicarbazide give acetaldehyde semicarbazone, the reaction will be</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/12db933e-e21c-4366-978c-cb26003abebb.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 302px;\"/></p><p>Hence the product formed has three nitrogen atoms in it.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
